### =========================================================================
### FraudWatch API - Interactive IntelliJ HTTP Client
### Click the little GREEN PLAY BUTTON (▶) next to any request to execute it!
### =========================================================================

### 1. View Dashboard Summary
GET http://localhost:8080/api/dashboard/summary
Accept: application/json

### 2. View All Accounts & Current Balances
GET http://localhost:8080/api/accounts
Accept: application/json

### 3. View All Active Fraud Detection Rules
GET http://localhost:8080/api/rules
Accept: application/json

### 4. Create Normal Transaction (Jane Smith sends ₹2,000 to John Doe -> Status: COMPLETED)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "senderAccountId": 2,
  "receiverAccountId": 1,
  "amount": 2000.00
}

### 5. Create Fraud Transaction (Exceeds ₹50,000 Threshold -> Status: FLAGGED)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "senderAccountId": 2,
  "receiverAccountId": 1,
  "amount": 55000.00
}

### 6. View All Transactions
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Accept: application/json

### 7. View Pending Flagged Transactions Waiting for Review
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reviews/pending
Accept: application/json

### 8. Approve a Flagged Transaction (Debit sender & Credit receiver now)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/reviews/6/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reviewer": "ComplianceOfficer",
  "reason": "Verified user KYC and confirmed high-value transfer authorization"
}

### 9. Block a Flagged Transaction (Permanently mark BLOCKED)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/reviews/6/block
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reviewer": "SecurityLead",
  "reason": "Suspicious rapid velocity activity detected and rejected"
}

### 10. View Fraud Rules Breakdown / Flagged Counts
GET http://localhost:8080/api/dashboard/flagged-by-rule
Accept: application/json
